{
  "title": "__SYSTEM_NAME__",
  "uid": "system-__SYSTEM_ID__",
  "annotations": {
    "list": [
      {
        "builtIn": 1,
        "datasource": {
          "type": "grafana",
          "uid": "-- Grafana --"
        },
        "enable": true,
        "hide": false,
        "iconColor": "rgba(255, 96, 96, 1)",
        "name": "Annotations & Alerts",
        "type": "dashboard"
      }
    ]
  },
  "tags": [
    "onboarding",
    "__SYSTEM_TYPE__"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "env",
        "label": "Environment",
        "type": "custom",
        "query": "__ENV_OPTIONS__",
        "current": {},
        "multi": false,
        "includeAll": false,
        "hide": 0
      },
      {
        "name": "host",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": "__DATASOURCE_MIMIR__",
        "query": "label_values(target_info, host_name)",
        "refresh": 2,
        "multi": true,
        "includeAll": true,
        "current": {
          "text": "All",
          "value": "$__all"
        },
        "description": "Filters every per-host panel below. Matters once this tenant has more than a handful of Linux hosts - a timeseries with one line per host, or a table with one row per host, stops being readable well before real fleet scale (thousands of hosts). Narrow this down instead of leaving it on All."
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "title": "System",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 8,
        "h": 7
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**__SYSTEM_NAME__** (`__SYSTEM_ID__`, type `__SYSTEM_TYPE__`)\n\nTenant: `__TENANT_ID__`\n\nOwner: __OWNER_TEAM__ (__OWNER_CONTACT__)\n\n__DEMO_NARRATIVE__"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Configured Ingestion Budget",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 8,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 9,
        "h": 7
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "__BUDGET_TABLE__\n\nRendered from the manifest at generation time - not a live query. See **Ingestion Budget Usage** alongside for the live percentage."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "title": "Ingestion Budget Usage (per Signal)",
      "description": "This tenant's real ingested volume since local midnight (Europe/Zurich), as a percentage of EACH signal's own daily budget - Metrics (Mimir), Logs (Loki), Traces (Tempo), Profiles (Pyroscope) each shown as its own line. Both values read directly from two gauges scripts/ingestion-midnight-snapshot.py pushes every 2 minutes (demo_ingestion_since_midnight, demo_ingestion_daily_budget) - no subtraction on this panel's own side (NFR-05 SECOND pre-test audit round, fixed here: this used to recompute \"current minus a separately-pushed day-start snapshot\" in this panel's OWN PromQL, independently of - and able to silently disagree with - the enforcer's own decision, with its own version of that script's pre-fix reset-insensitivity; both now read the exact same, already-correct value). Green below 80%, yellow 80-90%, red above 90%. Same formula as the Operator: Tenant Ingestion Budget dashboard's own panel, filtered to this one tenant. Queried via the Mimir-anonymous datasource, not __DATASOURCE_MIMIR__ - see README.md's Multi-Tenancy section for why (self-monitoring metrics land under the anonymous tenant).",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "Mimir-anonymous",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 17,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 7,
        "h": 7
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 120,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 80
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 90
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "single"
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": false,
          "expr": "100 * demo_ingestion_since_midnight{tenant=~\"__TENANT_ID__\"} / on(tenant, signal) demo_ingestion_daily_budget{tenant=~\"__TENANT_ID__\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{signal}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "title": "Linux Hosts",
      "description": "One row per Linux host reporting under this tenant (target_info, the hostmetrics receiver's resource-attributes-as-labels). OS name/version come from /etc/os-release on the host, see instrumentation/platforms/linux/config.yaml.",
      "type": "table",
      "datasource": "__DATASOURCE_MIMIR__",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 10,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "organize",
          "options": {
            "excludeByName": {
              "Time": true,
              "Value": true,
              "__name__": true,
              "job": true,
              "os_type": true,
              "otel_scope_name": true,
              "otel_scope_version": true
            },
            "indexByName": {},
            "renameByName": {
              "host_name": "Host",
              "os_name": "OS Name",
              "os_version": "OS Version"
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "target_info{host_name=~\"$host\"}",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "title": "OS Release by Major Version",
      "description": "Lifecycle overview: how many hosts are on which major OS release. Extracted from os_version (e.g. \"9.4\" -> \"9\") via label_replace, joined with os_name.",
      "type": "piechart",
      "datasource": "__DATASOURCE_MIMIR__",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 10,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 7,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "values": [
            "value",
            "percent"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "count by (os_release_major) (label_join(label_replace(target_info{host_name=~\"$host\", os_name!=\"\"}, \"os_major_num\", \"$1\", \"os_version\", \"([0-9]+)\\\\..*\"), \"os_release_major\", \" \", \"os_name\", \"os_major_num\"))",
          "legendFormat": "{{os_release_major}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "title": "OS Release by Version",
      "description": "Lifecycle overview one level below major version: how many hosts are on which exact release (e.g. \"Rocky Linux 9.4\").",
      "type": "piechart",
      "datasource": "__DATASOURCE_MIMIR__",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 17,
        "y": 7,
        "w": 7,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "right",
          "values": [
            "value",
            "percent"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true,
          "expr": "count by (os_release) (label_join(target_info{host_name=~\"$host\", os_name!=\"\"}, \"os_release\", \" \", \"os_name\", \"os_version\"))",
          "legendFormat": "{{os_release}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "title": "CPU Utilization by Host",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "__DATASOURCE_MIMIR__",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 15,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "100 * (1 - (sum by (host_name) (rate(system_cpu_time_seconds_total{state=\"idle\", host_name=~\"$host\"}[$__rate_interval])) / sum by (host_name) (rate(system_cpu_time_seconds_total{host_name=~\"$host\"}[$__rate_interval]))))",
          "legendFormat": "{{host_name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "title": "Memory Usage by Host",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "__DATASOURCE_MIMIR__",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 15,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "100 * system_memory_usage_bytes{state=\"used\", host_name=~\"$host\"} / on(host_name) group_left() sum by (host_name) (system_memory_usage_bytes{host_name=~\"$host\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{host_name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "title": "Filesystem Usage by Host/Mountpoint",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "__DATASOURCE_MIMIR__",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 23,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 100
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "100 * system_filesystem_usage_bytes{state=\"used\", host_name=~\"$host\"} / on(host_name, mountpoint, device) group_left() sum by (host_name, mountpoint, device) (system_filesystem_usage_bytes{host_name=~\"$host\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{host_name}} {{mountpoint}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "title": "Disk I/O by Host",
      "type": "timeseries",
      "datasource": "__DATASOURCE_MIMIR__",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 12,
        "y": 23,
        "w": 12,
        "h": 8
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "Bps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (host_name) (rate(system_disk_io_bytes_total{host_name=~\"$host\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{host_name}}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "title": "Recent Logs",
      "description": "Queries by service_name, not k8s_namespace_name - this is a VM (journald/syslog), not a Kubernetes pod, so it has no k8s_* labels at all. Not filtered by $host - Loki's log stream doesn't carry a reliable host_name label the way Mimir's metrics do.",
      "type": "logs",
      "datasource": "__DATASOURCE_LOKI__",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 31,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 8
      },
      "options": {
        "showTime": true,
        "wrapLogMessage": true,
        "sortOrder": "Descending"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "{service_name=~\".+\"}"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
